@flexiarg snatch/widen-the-cascade-only-on-evidence
@title Widen the Cascade Only on Evidence
@audience policy authors
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/have-a-temperament
@see-also cascades/on-the-fly-cascade

! conclusion: The cautious temperament starts from the patterns that fire, admits one more only when the last admission paid, and states the rule that stops the widening.

  + context: **Policy grain.** Operand: cascade membership. Snatch's `organise`
    takes the **full** transitive `@why` closure of the acting set
    (`checks/playout_snatch.clj:248-257`); a temperament that widens gradually
    is the other end of the same axis, and neither end is chosen by anything
    today.

  + IF:
    You are building a cascade rather than being handed one.

  + HOWEVER:
    Both ends fail, in opposite directions. The temperament alone is too little
    to play from; the full closure is too much — in the g4/snatcher run three
    patterns acted and four more were added by closure, so more than half the
    cascade was present because it was stood on and never fired
    (`checks/snatch-cascade.edn`). In an eighteen-pattern fixture that is
    bounded. Over the eighty-five-pattern repository no bound is stated
    anywhere.

  + THEN:
    Admit patterns one at a time, ordered by what the previous admission bought,
    and stop on a rule stated in advance — a marginal-gain floor, a budget, or
    saturation. Record the rule and where it stopped on the cascade with the
    run.

  + BECAUSE:
    A cascade with no stopping rule has its size decided by the shape of the
    authority graph rather than by the run. The stopping rule is what makes
    "which patterns" a policy decision instead of a graph property, and it is
    what lets two temperaments differ on the same repository.
    + evidence: the loop already exists and the substrate does not.
      `futon3a/holes/labs/M-memes-arrows/cascade_construct.py:222-232` is greedy
      by marginal coverage with `if chosen and m < epsilon: break`, and
      `cascade_serve.py:21-27` applies a budget ceiling downstream. Its
      relevance term is embedding cosine (`cascade_construct.py:48-58`), which
      law O2 refuses — edges are authored, *"never inferred from similarity,
      co-occurrence or prose"* (`P-validated-R5.md:500`). So it supplies the
      loop and the stop, and no part of what is being ordered.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - What replaces embedding relevance with a measure read off the authored
      `@why`/`@how` landscape is open, and is not decided here.
